Every triple contains an edge, so $\alpha = 2$. $\square$

### 5. Domination number $\gamma = 2$

The set $\{0, 2\}$ is dominating: vertex $0$ covers $\{0,1,3\}$, vertex $2$ covers $\{1,2,3,4\}$. Union $= \{0,1,2,3,4\} = V$.

No single vertex dominates all of $V$:
